## Governor 1 — Myostatin: the speed limiter

**Myostatin** is the genetic growth brake — evolution's cap so you don't over-build. It doesn't decide whether one meal becomes muscle; it limits the *rate and ceiling* of accretion across a block. Mechanical tension transiently lowers it; high-dose androgens lower it further; and dedicated tools ([[YK-11 (30mg-ml ×10ml) — aminotech|YK-11]], follistatin derivatives) crush it hardest. Lower the brake and the ceiling and speed of myofibrillar hypertrophy both rise.

> [!caution] Brake removal is not construction
> Suppressing myostatin without the stimulus, substrate, and recovery underneath it is removing the speed limiter from a parked car. Sequence matters: build the engine (tension), supply the fuel (aminos, energy, permissive mTOR), *then* de-restrict.

