## Governor 2 — The osmolality loop (pump → growth)

The "pump" isn't just aesthetics, and it isn't only a downstream result — it's a **feed-forward loop** that touches Link 1 and Link 2 at the same time. Forcing fluid into the cell with carbohydrate, sodium, creatine, betaine, glycerol, and water stretches the membrane taut, and the cell reads that internal pressure as a structural emergency it must reinforce:

```
 carbs + sodium + creatine/betaine/glycerol + water
        ──► cell swelling / pump
              ├─► better training output ............ (feeds Link 1)
              ├─► mTORC1-permissive volume signal .... (feeds Link 2)
              └─► sarcoplasmic expansion ............. (fills Compartment B)
                       └─► supports the next hard session
```

So the pump helps you train harder, supports the growth switch, *and* fills the energy/fluid compartment that lets the harder training keep happening — ==Compartment B (fluid) ends up directly triggering Compartment A (structure).== The OTC levers are cheap and real: [[Creatine Monohydrate (1000g) — Shopee|creatine]] (~5 g/day, the cornerstone phosphagen + cell-volumizer), [[TMG (Betaine) (750mg×120tab) — iHerb|betaine/TMG]] (~2.5 g/day osmolyte + methyl donor), [[Glycerol (1000g) — Shopee|glycerol]] and [[L-Citrulline (1000g) — Shopee|citrulline]] for hyperhydration and perfusion, and the boring base of carbs, sodium, potassium-rich food, and enough water.

