## Monitoring & red flags

Pulls from [[Bloodwork & Calculated Biomarkers]] and the protection protocols; the off-season-specific watch list.

- **Waist vs lifts** — the partitioning readout, *and* the distension-ceiling trigger: waist expanding disproportionately to performance (or appetite vanishing + waking glucose drifting) means you've hit your ceiling — stop the surplus and run a sharp mini-cut ([[Off-Season Mini-Cut Protocol]]) back to the floor. Pick a hard number in advance (a waist measurement or body-fat mark), don't rely only on biofeedback.
- **Fasting & post-meal glucose** — especially where GH/MK-677, high food, and low activity stack. The growth block's quiet failure mode is becoming a fat-gain block; hand to [[Glucose & Insulin Sensitivity Protocol]] early.
- **GI & inflammation signals** — stool consistency, bloating, appetite drift, and a heavy/inflamed feeling are the *early warning* for the Governor 3 gut bottleneck, well before it shows up as degraded glucose numbers. Catch it here and you protect insulin sensitivity before it breaks.
- **Estradiol — don't crush it.** E2 is anabolic and joint/IGF-supportive; over-suppressing an AI in a bulk limits growth (the [[Part 3.0 - The Eight Anabolic Pathways|Pathway 3]] trap).
- **Sleep & recovery** — protect **slow-wave (deep) sleep** specifically: it carries the night's GH/IGF-1 pulses and glymphatic clearance, so wrecking it cuts growth signalling, not just rest — on top of raising cortisol and worsening glucose. Hits Links 1, 3, and 5 at once.
- **BP / edema / hematocrit / lipids** — where androgen, GH, and high-carb/high-sodium tools overlap; per [[Blood Pressure & Fluid Escalation Protocol]] and [[Lipid Management Protocol]].
- **Pump vs cramp** — pump is useful; cramping, dizziness, or palpitations are an electrolyte/hydration warning, not a badge.
- **Insulin red flags** — shaking, sweating, confusion, faintness, or severe hunger after any glucose-lowering tool is a stop-everything, fast-carb event (hard gate in [[Bulk Recovery & Partitioning Protocol]]).

